<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Feb producer prices rise 2.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Feb producer prices rise 2.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch producer price index (PPI) for manufactured goods fell a provisional 0.2 percent in February from January, giving a 2.5 percent rise year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p> DUTCH PRODUCER PRICES	   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		103.3	 103.5	100.8</p>
<p> Month-on-month pct change     -0.2	  +0.5	 +0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year pct change	  2.5	   2.9	 -0.4</p>
<p> Subindex domestic prices     106.8	 106.9	105.1</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		  +1.6	  +1.9	 +0.9</p>
<p> Subindex export prices	 100.6	 100.9	 97.5</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		  +3.2	  +3.7	 -1.3</p>
<p>The CBS said that the month-on-month fall in domestic and export producer prices mainly reflected a strong decline in petrochemicals product prices, which fell by 6.5 percent.</p>
<p>In other sectors prices rose slightly, it said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
